@startuml
' purpose: distinguish obsolete plaintext OpenCode credential references from active native logins and session-history compatibility
' covers: defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh
' covers: defs/opencode/harness.manifest
' covers: defs/cursor/harness.manifest
' covers: defs/codex/harness.manifest
' covers: defs/claudecode/harness.manifest
' covers: defs/hermes/harness.manifest
' covers: defs/cecli/harness.manifest
' covers: internal/credentials/credentials.go
' covers: internal/contract/opencode_credentials_test.go
' covers: packages/lib/proveo-opencode-runtime
' covers: packages/lib/opencode-credentials.py
' covers: packages/lib/test_opencode_cache.py
' covers: packages/lib/test_opencode_runtime_native.py
' status: source audit complete; Executor selected obsolete references only.
' OpenCode V2 stores native provider/account credentials in SQLite; its old auth.json startup message is removed.
' Remove unused history-merge/digest functions and their unused environment forwarding without adding implicit imports.
' Keep auth.json and mcp-auth.json snapshot exclusions as import-sanitization safeguards, not plaintext persistence features.
' Keep OpenCode V1-session records inside adopted V2 databases listable and resumable with the pinned native executable.
' Preserve native schema migration records and explicit history-source preparation.
' Cursor declares .cursor/auth.json denial; this is its active native path, not obsolete OpenCode storage.
' Codex recognizes .codex/auth.json and intentionally persists native subscription login; do not remove it in this cleanup.
' Claude Code recognizes .claude/.credentials.json and retains .claude; do not change its active login policy.
' Hermes and cecli declare no auth-file login lookup in the subscription login registry.
' This source audit does not inspect host tokens or establish the presence of any credential file on Executor hosts.
' Executor declined the separate Docker legacy-file exposure redesign; its whole-home mount remains outside this cleanup.
' Host-owned OpenCode OAuth remains planned in _spec/_paradigms/opencode-oauth-persistence.puml.
title Harness credential-storage audit — obsolete references only
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
actor Executor
component "OpenCode V2\nSQLite authentication\nexplicit history preparation" as OC
component "Cursor\nactive auth.json denial" as CURSOR
component "Codex + Claude Code\nactive native login files" as LOGIN
component "Hermes + cecli\nno registered auth-file login lookup" as KEYS
Executor --> OC : remove obsolete messaging/helpers
Executor --> CURSOR : retain active behavior
Executor --> LOGIN : retain active behavior
Executor --> KEYS : no matching obsolete reference
note bottom of OC
  Credential cleanup does not remove session
  compatibility or native schema migrations.
  Adopted V1 sessions retain their transcripts.
end note
@enduml
